        {
          "id": 2830896614,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Thanks for the feedback, it is not a finished work (as the print_ function wasn't added) and all feedback is appreciated. In fact, the fields I added some time ago (`tcp.stream.(client|server).contiguity_count`) are somewhat biased as they rely on client==src but at the end they are sufficient for determining if the capture has missing parts or not. The idea with this new MR is to make them more reliable and intuitive, and when the connection handshake is missing probably we won't do that much with the capture and jump to another one.\n\nI will try to integrate your feedback to enhance the MR, but it's not all obvious although your words are quite clear (ex: \n> maybe this is useful in a much broader scope than just for tcp connections)\n\nThanks again",
          "author": {
            "id": 6797213,
            "username": "eugene.adell",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Eugène Adell",
            "state": "active",
