        {
          "id": 2831080873,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Sorry, maybe I wasn't clear. I thought tracking which endpoint is a client an which is a server, could be useful for a lot of other things as well. I don't have many examples, but if we make it available maybe people will find some nice use for it.\n\nOne idea I have is that in the conversation view, we can display conversations for a lot of different transports. We already show how many packets and bytes go in each direction. Maybe if we KNOW which of the two endpoints is the client and which is the server we could indicate it in the conversation list. If we know which is which, we could make sure to always show the client as AddressA, and always shows the server as AddressB. Maybe use it for display filters so you could say \"smb && client\" or similar to only show packets that were sent by a client and were also smb.\n\nMaybe this is completely out of scope for this MR. It just tickled me and I thought, it could be neat to be able to always know if this is a packet sent by the client or the server. Maybe someone will use this information to create some really clever new feature. Maybe just ignore it for this MR and we can think about it for a separate issue.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7014716,
