        {
          "id": 2832020263,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Thanks for taking the time for writing all this, the ideas suggested would help in many cases indeed. That looks like abstracting the Source (or Destination) IP address, enabling a new filter style rather than building filters on real IP addresses as we always did. If we had to think of other layers (Ethernet) / protocols (ICMP) that could also bring some headache (when ICMP contains the first bytes of a TCP segment), in this case it's necessary to decide if _client_ is unique to the packet or a generalized protocol field (following the _Stream ID_ which needed to be reused in several protocols)\n\nAbout the _Conversations Statistics_ dialog, I would let the user decide if he wants things ordered by time (Address A = first Src Address seen) or by the Client-Server relationship you said (Address A = Client Address), but that's maybe too much for a first MR.\n\nI think we can use this MR to build around the ideas described, its implementation can take some time though.",
          "author": {
